1
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:08,170
Hello? Is that you, Chiba?

2
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:10,830
Huh? A movie?

3
00:00:10,830 --> 00:00:14,710
Sorry, I've got plans to hit up
a recording studio with some friends.

4
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:19,580
Huh? But it's our day off.
We're free to do whatever, aren't we?

5
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:22,630
Besides, only couples go 
to movies alone together.

6
00:00:22,630 --> 00:00:24,080
I'm gonna hang up now.

7
00:00:25,670 --> 00:00:30,710
Good grief, Chiba really needs
to get a girlfriend to go to the movies with.

8
00:00:30,710 --> 00:00:34,460
All right. It's time to show 
Naopei just how awesome I am.

9
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:37,130
Yo! If it isn't, Kabachi.

10
00:00:37,130 --> 00:00:38,790
What are you doing out here?

11
00:00:38,790 --> 00:00:40,290
Huh? Tokiwa?!

12
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:41,880
Headed to practice?

13
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:45,580
That's weird, most teams usually take
the last day of Golden Week off.

14
00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:47,750
So why aren't you guys doing the same?

15
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,330
M-mind your own business!
Not everybody has it as easy as you!

16
00:00:51,330 --> 00:00:54,460
That flippant attitude of yours 
really gets under my skin!

17
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:56,840
I know we lost to your 
team in the last tourney,

18
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:59,340
but my I scored way more 
points than you overall.

19
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:00,920
Don't get too cocky.

20
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:02,960
Well yeah, I'm a point guard.

21
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:08,210
Oh, and by the way, I managed to pull off
a triple-double in that match.

22
00:01:08,210 --> 00:01:11,040
For points, assists, and 
steals, if I remember right.

23
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:14,580
So tell me, why are you guys headed this way?

24
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:16,500
Let me guess, is it a practice match?

25
00:01:19,330 --> 00:01:21,290
A practice match with Kuzu High?

26
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:23,500
Really? Kuzu High, huh?

27
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:25,020
What's your problem?!

28
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:27,140
Don't look down on us
like we've fallen from grace or something!

29
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:29,360
I swear, you're one of 
the rudest jerks I know!

30
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:32,920
We're just going for kicks 
and giggles, that's all.

31
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:35,670
You know there's no way I'd get serious
against trash like Kuzu High.

32
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,960
Uh-huh, sure.

33
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:39,750
QUIT GIVING ME THAT LOOK, DAMMIT!

34
00:01:39,750 --> 00:01:43,290
Taro always blows his top at guys
who have better looks than him, huh?

35
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:46,420
Well, there is some truth 
to what he was saying.

36
00:01:46,830 --> 00:01:50,130
I don't think we'll need to put too much effort
into this game against Kuzu High.

37
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:52,080
Oh, I just remembered, Konishi.

38
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:54,460
Don't you have a relative 
who's getting married today?

39
00:01:54,710 --> 00:01:56,420
You should've just taken 
the day off and went.

40
00:01:57,330 --> 00:01:58,580
It's fine.

41
00:01:59,170 --> 00:02:02,040
I've actually been looking 
forward to playing Kuzu High.

42
00:02:25,080 --> 00:02:31,210
Ahiru no Sora

43
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:41,920
The Boys' Spirit

44
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:41,750
I'm sorry that it took so long.

45
00:03:41,750 --> 00:03:45,630
I told you they'd be ready in time for the game,
but this is cutting it super close.

46
00:03:45,630 --> 00:03:47,750
This is awesome! They're as good as new!

47
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:50,290
And I can't believe how clean they are now!

48
00:03:50,290 --> 00:03:53,500
Yeah, we gave them a thorough cleaning.

49
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:55,380
But maybe that was going too far.

50
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:57,330
No way! This is great!

51
00:03:57,330 --> 00:03:59,250
Now I won't get a hard 
time for how they look!

52
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:01,130
Great, I'm glad to hear it.

53
00:04:01,130 --> 00:04:03,250
So, you don't need mine anymore, right?

54
00:04:03,250 --> 00:04:04,790
Oh, yeah.

55
00:04:10,330 --> 00:04:11,790
Uh, can you wait just a sec?

56
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:16,920
Sorry, Nanao. Would you mind if I used those
for just one more day?

57
00:04:17,080 --> 00:04:20,080
Huh? But we finally fixed up your old ones...

58
00:04:20,290 --> 00:04:23,290
Yeah, but yours were really comfy to wear.

59
00:04:23,580 --> 00:04:24,580
And more importantly,

60
00:04:24,830 --> 00:04:30,040
I went through our whole training camp alongside
those shoes, so I want to use them until the end!

61
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,790
Kurumatani...

62
00:04:33,330 --> 00:04:34,380
Are you sure?

63
00:04:34,670 --> 00:04:37,920
Of course, as long as you're fine with it.

64
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:40,290
Okay, then please feel free to use them.

65
00:04:40,290 --> 00:04:42,290
Uh, right, thanks very much.

66
00:04:43,330 --> 00:04:45,330
What are you two even doing?

67
00:04:45,330 --> 00:04:47,000
Kitasumi High is here!

68
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,710
Yo. Sorry to keep you guys waiting.

69
00:04:54,170 --> 00:04:56,580
Wait, is that Tokiwa? But why?

70
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:57,380
Hey.

71
00:04:58,380 --> 00:05:00,540
Why the hell did you tag along?!

72
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:01,630
Just felt like it.

73
00:05:01,580 --> 00:05:03,540
Salt

74
00:05:01,630 --> 00:05:03,630
Be gone, demon! Be gone!

75
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:06,080
Oh come on, let me be a spectator.

76
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:07,920
I promise that I won't get in the way.

77
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:11,460
Your mere presence causes enough problems
by taking everyone's eyes off of me!

78
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:12,540
So just get lost!

79
00:05:12,540 --> 00:05:13,540
Seriously?

80
00:05:13,540 --> 00:05:16,630
Don't be so mean, I ditched my band practice
just so I could come.

81
00:05:16,630 --> 00:05:18,920
Hello again, Hanazono. It's been a long time.

82
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:21,210
Isn't that Konishi?

83
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:23,670
Huh? I don't think I know this guy.

84
00:05:23,670 --> 00:05:26,420
Back in middle school, 
he was a grade below us.

85
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:28,540
That weird kid who was always 
tagging along with us.

86
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:31,170
Oh! Lil' Koni!

87
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:34,290
But damn, you must've 
really hit a growth spurt.

88
00:05:34,290 --> 00:05:35,540
How tall are you now?

89
00:05:35,540 --> 00:05:37,830
196 centimeters, if you can believe it.

90
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,210
Oh yeah? So, I guess you kept 
playing basketball, huh?

91
00:05:41,210 --> 00:05:43,330
Yes. Thanks to your help.

92
00:05:43,540 --> 00:05:46,250
Thanks to us? I don't even 
remember doing anything.

93
00:05:46,580 --> 00:05:50,710
I used to join you both
during your extended practice sessions at night.

94
00:05:50,710 --> 00:05:53,210
Back then, I had no basketball 
skills to speak of...

95
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:57,250
Momoharu would often take time
to teach me a variety of things.

96
00:05:57,250 --> 00:05:58,380
And what about me?

97
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:03,040
Well Chiaki, you would always have me
fetch your snacks... and pay for them.

98
00:06:03,210 --> 00:06:05,130
Goddammit, Chikai...

99
00:06:06,420 --> 00:06:11,830
After you two left the team, most everybody else
just stopped taking the game seriously.

100
00:06:11,830 --> 00:06:13,290
It was depressing.

101
00:06:13,670 --> 00:06:18,250
But actually, from then until now,
I've never skipped a day of practice!

102
00:06:19,330 --> 00:06:21,210
Wow, you're a real workaholic!

103
00:06:21,210 --> 00:06:23,040
Nice, man. Keep it up.

104
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:23,880
Y-yes, sir!

105
00:06:27,130 --> 00:06:28,420
Senpai...

106
00:06:28,420 --> 00:06:29,080
Huh?

107
00:06:29,420 --> 00:06:32,670
Basketball isn't some merciful sport
that you can just crawl back to...

108
00:06:33,420 --> 00:06:35,460
...after you made the choice to drop out.

109
00:06:35,830 --> 00:06:36,790
What?!

110
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:40,130
Say that again, punk.

111
00:06:40,130 --> 00:06:41,380
Stop it, Momoharu.
This time to my face!

112
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,170
If you want to prove him wrong,
then do it out on the court.

113
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:49,040
Okay, then, please use this as a locker room.

114
00:06:49,750 --> 00:06:52,960
If there's anything you need help with,
please feel free to ask.

115
00:06:53,290 --> 00:06:55,960
She's a... major cutie!

116
00:06:56,460 --> 00:06:59,920
You know, girls like her always 
make the best managers!

117
00:07:00,130 --> 00:07:02,920
Actually, it seems that she's
a member of the girls' team here.

118
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,880
Yeah, we already know their manager.

119
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:06,580
Isn't it supposed to be Taro's cousin?

120
00:07:06,580 --> 00:07:07,330
Huh?

121
00:07:07,580 --> 00:07:09,330
Speaking of, where'd he run off to?

122
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:16,790
I want to use them until the end!

123
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:23,630
What are you sitting here 
hugging your shoes for?

124
00:07:23,630 --> 00:07:24,830
Ouch!

125
00:07:27,250 --> 00:07:29,750
Wait, I don't remember you 
using shoes like those.

126
00:07:29,750 --> 00:07:31,630
Uh, yeah, these are actually...

127
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:34,130
Whatever.

128
00:07:34,130 --> 00:07:36,880
Anyway, I just wanted to make sure
you haven't forgotten our promise.

129
00:07:37,420 --> 00:07:39,000
What promise?

130
00:07:39,210 --> 00:07:43,040
Oh, don't be coy. We made a promise to go
to the amusement park together, right?

131
00:07:43,040 --> 00:07:45,710
Yeah, but that was only if I found the time.

132
00:07:45,710 --> 00:07:49,040
Oh please, you gave me that same line
during spring vacation.

133
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:52,540
Besides, places like that are usually for dates
and we're cousins.

134
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:54,630
It doesn't matter if we're cousins.

135
00:07:55,420 --> 00:07:58,170
I am.... dead serious 
about my feelings for you!

136
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,710
Stop being weird and giving 
me that look, you jerk!

137
00:08:03,710 --> 00:08:04,830
It's creeping me out!

138
00:08:04,830 --> 00:08:06,540
She's so adorable.

139
00:08:06,670 --> 00:08:09,790
Oh, there you are! Hey, Nanao! 
I've been looking for you.

140
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:11,040
What is it?

141
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:12,750
Mr. Satsuki needs you.

142
00:08:13,080 --> 00:08:15,710
The coach for the other 
team came to greet us.

143
00:08:14,250 --> 00:08:15,710
That's the shorty from before...

144
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:18,670
I recognize those shoes!

145
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:32,580
Whoa, what are they doing?

146
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:34,250
Looks like a circus performance.

147
00:08:34,250 --> 00:08:35,630
That's a tip drill.

148
00:08:36,080 --> 00:08:38,170
Anybody can do it with some simple practice.

149
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:40,330
They're so organized.

150
00:08:40,330 --> 00:08:42,630
Yo, have you guys improved a bit?

151
00:08:42,630 --> 00:08:43,960
Hey, Tokiwa.

152
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:45,080
We have!

153
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:48,380
I think if we played your team at Maru High again,
things would turn out differently!

154
00:08:48,750 --> 00:08:50,630
I welcome the challenge.

155
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:54,210
Just so you know, the team that you're facing today
is strong in their own right.

156
00:08:54,630 --> 00:08:55,880
So I've heard.

157
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:58,540
Their match against you guys
went all the way to overtime.

158
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:01,500
Our team's roster is heavily 
comprised of seniors.

159
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:04,290
But Kitasumi relies more
upon freshman and sophomore players,

160
00:09:04,290 --> 00:09:06,170
which means they're only 
going to get stronger.

161
00:09:06,630 --> 00:09:10,080
It's hard to say that we could win a second time
if we had to face them again.

162
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:11,830
And above all...

163
00:09:11,830 --> 00:09:13,830
...he's the player you really 
need to be careful of.

164
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:18,580
He may not exactly look it,
but his talent for basketball is top-tier.

165
00:09:19,250 --> 00:09:23,040
Especially when it comes to points,
he's always the one who scores the most.

166
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:27,420
To be frank, I don't think I stand a chance
against him in a one-on-one.

167
00:09:27,580 --> 00:09:29,040
Even you, Tokiwa?

168
00:09:29,210 --> 00:09:32,920
In fact, that guy alone managed
to score 50 points against our team.

169
00:09:33,460 --> 00:09:37,000
I imagine what will decide the outcome of this game
is whether you can stop him or not.

170
00:09:37,210 --> 00:09:38,500
50 points...

171
00:09:39,920 --> 00:09:41,250
Oops, sorry about that.

172
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:46,580
I'm hyped to play against 
someone so impressive!

173
00:09:46,580 --> 00:09:47,380
Here.

174
00:09:47,830 --> 00:09:50,500
I thought I'd let this be a 
learning experience for you.

175
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:52,670
But it turns out, I'm going 
to have to bring my A-game.

176
00:09:52,670 --> 00:09:53,670
Huh?

177
00:09:59,290 --> 00:10:02,380
Listen up, squirt! You're 
not on anybody's radar!

178
00:10:02,630 --> 00:10:04,170
The only winner here is me!

179
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:08,960
I'm not gonna lose!

180
00:10:09,710 --> 00:10:11,250
I'm really feeling it now, you know?

181
00:10:11,250 --> 00:10:13,830
This is so much more nerve wracking
than our Maru High match.

182
00:10:13,830 --> 00:10:14,880
You said it!

183
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:18,750
That's fine and all, but please tell me you guys
actually memorized the damn rules this time.

184
00:10:18,750 --> 00:10:20,580
Dude, I've got them all down pat!

185
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:23,210
We're not allowed to move 
while holding the ball.

186
00:10:23,210 --> 00:10:25,290
We're not allowed to do 
any punching or kicking.

187
00:10:25,670 --> 00:10:27,330
And, uh, what else was there?

188
00:10:27,830 --> 00:10:29,330
Perfect, just how I like it.

189
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:33,710
Well, that's a surprise. The other team
isn't wearing any uniforms at all.

190
00:10:34,210 --> 00:10:37,710
All right then, boys. I suppose you don't have
to bother wearing your uniforms, either.

191
00:10:38,040 --> 00:10:40,080
Huh? Are you sure about that, coach?

192
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:42,750
It makes us look silly
if we're the only ones going all out, right?

193
00:10:42,750 --> 00:10:45,420
Let's just get this over 
with and head home. Okay?

194
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:49,710
If you're going to be such a wet blanket,
then why did you even accept this match?

195
00:10:49,710 --> 00:10:53,290
Cut me some slack, Taro said he was going to quit
if I didn't go through with it.

196
00:10:53,290 --> 00:10:55,920
You guys wouldn't be happy
if Taro just left the team, right?

197
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:59,460
Anyway, take a look at that.

198
00:11:01,790 --> 00:11:06,040
Oh jeez, there's always at least one fool
who loves pretending that he's in the NBA.

199
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:09,750
And despite how they may look,
they always totally suck. Without fail.

200
00:11:09,750 --> 00:11:13,130
I mean, come on, are we supposed
to believe he's got a tattoo or somet-?

201
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:14,250
GREASED
LIGHTNING

202
00:11:17,710 --> 00:11:19,880
Uh, hello. What's up, Juri?

203
00:11:19,880 --> 00:11:22,170
Sorry, do you mind calling 
me back a little later?

204
00:11:22,540 --> 00:11:25,000
I've got really important plans right now.

205
00:11:29,750 --> 00:11:32,750
Basketball isn't some merciful sport
that you can just crawl back to...

206
00:11:33,630 --> 00:11:35,750
...after you made the choice to drop out.

207
00:11:36,710 --> 00:11:38,460
Damn cocky punk.

208
00:11:38,750 --> 00:11:41,710
Just you wait, I gonna 
make you eat those words!

209
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:44,790
I love you. Please go out with me.

210
00:11:45,250 --> 00:11:46,250
Huh?

211
00:11:46,630 --> 00:11:50,460
Oops, that came out wrong!
I was trying to say, "I'm gonna do my best!"

212
00:11:50,790 --> 00:11:53,710
You can just forget all about 
that other thing I said, okay?

213
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:56,500
Like really, don't worry your 
pretty little head about it.

214
00:11:56,670 --> 00:11:59,670
Seriously, for real, you don't 
need to even think it over!

215
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,630
Enough blabbering! Just get out there!

216
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:04,420
All right, I need to put my heart into this.

217
00:12:04,420 --> 00:12:06,040
For the sake of love.

218
00:12:06,420 --> 00:12:07,670
Hey Kurumatani!

219
00:12:07,670 --> 00:12:09,330
It's time to line up, hurry!

220
00:12:09,330 --> 00:12:11,330
Oh, sorry! I'm coming!

221
00:12:13,580 --> 00:12:14,710
Kurumatani.

222
00:12:15,330 --> 00:12:16,630
You can do it!

223
00:12:17,580 --> 00:12:19,380
Totally! Just you watch!

224
00:12:20,830 --> 00:12:23,380
Okay, everyone. We will now begin the match!

225
00:12:23,710 --> 00:12:25,830
I need all players to come 
to the center circle!

226
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:39,960
Kanagawa School of Medical Science
Secondary Hospital

227
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:39,710
Say, Ms. Yabuuchi?

228
00:12:40,290 --> 00:12:41,420
Yes?

229
00:12:42,210 --> 00:12:45,250
Do you think I could get permission
to leave here just for a bit?

230
00:12:45,250 --> 00:12:49,380
You already know that's impossible.
The doctor made that crystal clear, no?

231
00:12:49,710 --> 00:12:51,830
That's why I'm asking 
you. It'll be our secret.

232
00:12:51,830 --> 00:12:54,130
I promise to keep my mouth shut, okay?

233
00:12:54,130 --> 00:12:57,420
If I agreed to something like 
that I'd be fired immediately!

234
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,830
Is there something special 
that you have going on today?

235
00:13:00,830 --> 00:13:03,330
Uh... well, not really.

236
00:13:03,710 --> 00:13:06,000
It's nothing much, but even so.

237
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:13,040
I've got a game starting now...
gonna win for sure.

238
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:16,460
Get moving!

239
00:13:16,460 --> 00:13:17,460
All right!

240
00:13:22,330 --> 00:13:23,630
Whoa, so high!

241
00:13:24,790 --> 00:13:26,540
How do you like them apples?!

242
00:13:28,250 --> 00:13:30,960
Kuzu High #4! Jump ball violation!

243
00:13:31,330 --> 00:13:32,250
Huh?!

244
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:33,710
Momoharu...

245
00:13:33,710 --> 00:13:36,710
Hold up, what even makes that a foul?

246
00:13:36,710 --> 00:13:38,540
It was a violation, not a foul.

247
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:42,750
The ball must reach the apex of its toss
on a jump ball before anybody can touch it.

248
00:13:46,130 --> 00:13:48,960
Forget about it! We've 
only just gotten started!

249
00:13:48,960 --> 00:13:50,540
Keep your heads in the game!

250
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,580
Gah! They just scored one 
on us like it was nothing!

251
00:13:54,580 --> 00:13:55,750
Sorry, guys!

252
00:13:55,750 --> 00:13:57,420
You have to keep a closer 
eye on the other team!

253
00:13:57,670 --> 00:14:00,210
That was a perfect play. We 
knew this wouldn't be easy.

254
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:01,710
They're really good.

255
00:14:01,710 --> 00:14:04,210
Do we actually stand a chance against them?

256
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:07,880
You can do it, guys! Just remember
everything that we practiced!

257
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:08,960
Oh, right!

258
00:14:10,830 --> 00:14:12,880
It's our first possession, 
let's take it slow.

259
00:14:15,830 --> 00:14:18,330
A man-to-man defense from half-court, eh?

260
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,210
Incredible!

261
00:14:26,210 --> 00:14:29,130
Not only did he anticipate 
#11 throwing off the defense,

262
00:14:29,130 --> 00:14:32,790
but also that #4's movements would create
the perfect blind spot to get a pass through.

263
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:35,250
It bounced!

264
00:14:35,250 --> 00:14:36,380
You damn klutz!

265
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:40,670
That pass came at me way too hard,
learn how to hold back a little!

266
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:42,500
Don't let him shoot, Konishi!

267
00:14:42,790 --> 00:14:43,630
On it!

268
00:14:44,170 --> 00:14:45,630
Yes! I blocked him!

269
00:14:52,710 --> 00:14:55,000
He pulled a double clutch 
from that position?!

270
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:57,330
It looked like he was already halfway
behind the backboard!

271
00:14:58,130 --> 00:14:59,420
I don't believe it...

272
00:14:59,830 --> 00:15:01,580
So, they found a new forward?

273
00:15:01,580 --> 00:15:03,420
He's got a great feel for the game.

274
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:07,290
It's more than just their point guard,
the entire team has improved their offense.

275
00:15:08,460 --> 00:15:11,750
It's crazy to think they were essentially
just a team of amateurs until recently.

276
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:20,130
Sweet! Another basket for us!

277
00:15:21,830 --> 00:15:22,750
A steal!

278
00:15:22,750 --> 00:15:24,460
What was that, Katori?!

279
00:15:24,790 --> 00:15:27,080
You're doing a pretty 
solid job out there, Kite.

280
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:28,420
Remind me to pay you later.

281
00:15:28,920 --> 00:15:29,960
For real?

282
00:15:29,960 --> 00:15:33,170
Hold up! I just know you're gonna steal it
from my piggy bank again!

283
00:15:33,580 --> 00:15:36,880
Their center has a lot of jump height!
Don't let him in the paint!

284
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:40,290
Keep your eyes on #11 for sure!
Don't let him shake you off!

285
00:15:44,710 --> 00:15:46,290
That sign means...

286
00:15:48,670 --> 00:15:51,040
Setting up the Nabe Screen!

287
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:52,710
Taro! You've got a screen behind you!

288
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:53,670
Say what?

289
00:15:53,670 --> 00:15:55,130
Hmph, too easy.

290
00:15:55,380 --> 00:15:57,000
It'll take a lot more 
than that to shake me...

291
00:15:58,290 --> 00:15:59,290
He nailed it!

292
00:15:59,290 --> 00:16:00,750
Nice one, Nabe!

293
00:16:00,750 --> 00:16:03,500
Oh? They've really gotten 
themselves into good shape.

294
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:04,380
Switch!

295
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:07,670
Idiots. We're not gonna let such an obvious screen
get the better of us.

296
00:16:09,460 --> 00:16:10,290
He's fast!

297
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:16,930
I guess he wasn't just 
bragging when he said things

298
00:16:16,930 --> 00:16:19,120
would turn out differently 
if we played again.

299
00:16:23,290 --> 00:16:25,040
It seems that Kabachi has the right idea.

300
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:27,790
None of us can afford to be 
taking it easy right now.

301
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:33,170
Sakata, call us a timeout. Right now.

302
00:16:33,170 --> 00:16:35,500
Huh? But the game has barely started, sir!

303
00:16:35,790 --> 00:16:37,420
I know, it's fine.

304
00:16:39,380 --> 00:16:41,330
Timeout by Kitasumi High!

305
00:16:42,460 --> 00:16:44,080
What's the deal, coach?

306
00:16:44,080 --> 00:16:46,170
You realize we're barely a 
minute into the game, right?

307
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:48,960
Boys, go and put your uniforms back on.

308
00:16:50,080 --> 00:16:52,710
I'm benching our starting lineup
so you can all redo your warm-ups.

309
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:56,380
We won't... hold anything back.

310
00:16:57,580 --> 00:17:00,330
You're sure slow on the uptake, gramps.

311
00:17:00,330 --> 00:17:02,880
The coach should be the last one
to need a damn pep talk.

312
00:17:06,580 --> 00:17:09,710
We were ready to put everything
into this game from the very start!

313
00:17:11,130 --> 00:17:14,250
My apologies. I will admit this was a failure
on my part as your coach.

314
00:17:14,880 --> 00:17:17,580
I never expected to be 
bushwhacked so close to home.

315
00:17:17,580 --> 00:17:20,330
If we don't strike while the iron is hot,
it may come back to bite us.

316
00:17:21,630 --> 00:17:24,500
We'll start with man-to-man
and see how our opponent reacts.

317
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:26,830
Everyone make sure you know
who you're supposed to be guarding.

318
00:17:26,830 --> 00:17:28,040
I'm on #10!

319
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:29,790
I've got #6.

320
00:17:29,790 --> 00:17:33,750
None of the Kitasumi players are specialized
3-point shooters like Kurumatani,

321
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:35,710
so we can afford to ease 
up our defense a little.

322
00:17:36,130 --> 00:17:38,750
But please be wary of #7 in 
any and all circumstances.

323
00:17:38,750 --> 00:17:42,000
He won't hesitate to try and score
from both long and short range.

324
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:45,710
We have shut him down before 
he finds his sweet spot.

325
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:49,000
#7... That's who I'm guarding...

326
00:17:50,380 --> 00:17:52,130
The timeout has now ended!

327
00:17:52,130 --> 00:17:54,790
Okay! Let's really get this party started!

328
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:02,250
They've gotten serious about this.

329
00:18:02,580 --> 00:18:05,880
Which means everything before
was just a simple warm-up, huh?

330
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:08,630
Kitsumiyoshi | Kuzuryu

331
00:18:06,250 --> 00:18:08,040
Kitasumi ball! Throw-in!

332
00:18:08,830 --> 00:18:11,290
Nabe, stay on #10 as best you can!

333
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:12,960
Deny them any passes!

334
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:14,750
And make sure you stay alert for screens!

335
00:18:15,460 --> 00:18:16,880
I've got #7 all covered!

336
00:18:17,830 --> 00:18:19,750
So you're my defender, eh?

337
00:18:19,750 --> 00:18:22,210
Never thought I'd get matched 
up with such a shorty.

338
00:18:22,460 --> 00:18:24,080
You'll regret underestimating me.

339
00:18:24,420 --> 00:18:26,920
Oh please, you're the shortest one
on your entire team, Kabachi.

340
00:18:27,210 --> 00:18:29,380
That's enough of the pot 
calling the kettle black!

341
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:31,830
What irks me more are those shoes!

342
00:18:32,460 --> 00:18:33,330
My shoes?

343
00:18:34,170 --> 00:18:36,250
Yeah, I remember them from a year ago...

344
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:40,130
Hey, I recognize those. They're 
a limited-edition color.

345
00:18:40,130 --> 00:18:43,920
Yeah, but I'm worried that 
they look tacky on me.

346
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:47,080
Why worry about that? I think 
they look just fine on you.

347
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:48,330
Really?!

348
00:18:49,880 --> 00:18:51,540
That makes me happy! Thanks!

349
00:18:52,290 --> 00:18:53,630
KAPOW!

350
00:18:53,630 --> 00:18:56,000
Up until then, she had just been
one of my childish cousins.

351
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:59,000
But after that moment,
she became a woman inside my heart.

352
00:19:00,290 --> 00:19:02,000
Taro! You're holding onto 
the ball for too long!

353
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,460
The shot clock will run out!

354
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:08,290
I consider those shoes a gift from an angel above,
who led me to true love!

355
00:19:08,790 --> 00:19:10,540
And now this little bastard...

356
00:19:10,540 --> 00:19:12,500
...has his dirty feet all over them!

357
00:19:13,290 --> 00:19:14,500
I'll win them back.

358
00:19:14,830 --> 00:19:16,380
And rekindle the memories of our love!

359
00:19:17,130 --> 00:19:19,130
Awesome! A between-the-legs dribble!

360
00:19:23,710 --> 00:19:25,460
Between-the-legs into a spin.

361
00:19:25,790 --> 00:19:27,170
It's the same move he used before!

362
00:19:27,170 --> 00:19:28,130
No, wait!

363
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:35,130
He's gonna charge in! Don't let him through!

364
00:19:36,420 --> 00:19:38,500
He went straight for a jump shot?!

365
00:19:41,250 --> 00:19:42,790
And boom goes the dynamite!

366
00:19:44,170 --> 00:19:46,080
24-second violation!

367
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:47,920
The basket doesn't count!

368
00:19:48,250 --> 00:19:49,670
What?! No way!

369
00:19:49,670 --> 00:19:51,250
Are you sure I just didn't barely make it?!

370
00:19:51,420 --> 00:19:53,880
Ugh, I was so close! Dammit!

371
00:19:54,290 --> 00:19:55,380
Quit yapping so much.

372
00:19:55,540 --> 00:19:58,500
Am I crazy, or did he just 
blow a kiss to somebody?

373
00:19:58,500 --> 00:20:01,080
If he hadn't wasted time, that 
shot would have counted...

374
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:03,790
No kidding, one of those spins 
was totally unnecessary...

375
00:20:05,170 --> 00:20:06,500
Play with style.

376
00:20:06,630 --> 00:20:08,080
That's my motto, you know!

377
00:20:10,540 --> 00:20:12,540
That was a really clean cut to the middle.

378
00:20:12,750 --> 00:20:16,960
Not to mention that he actually looked away
from the basket, but still sunk the shot.

379
00:20:17,380 --> 00:20:19,460
I guess he's not just the 
idiot he seems to be.

380
00:20:19,920 --> 00:20:21,080
He's good.

381
00:20:21,670 --> 00:20:22,670
Uh-oh.

382
00:20:22,670 --> 00:20:24,080
Sorry, that came up short!

383
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:25,250
Rebound!

384
00:20:27,710 --> 00:20:29,670
Glad to see you're pulling 
your weight, Senpai!

385
00:20:29,670 --> 00:20:30,920
Oh, shut up!

386
00:20:31,290 --> 00:20:32,710
Nice one, Kite!

387
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:34,460
Kitsumiyoshi | Kuzuryu

388
00:20:32,710 --> 00:20:34,460
That puts us ahead by 5!

389
00:20:34,460 --> 00:20:36,420
Yo. What's the matter, Konishi?

390
00:20:36,630 --> 00:20:40,330
You were talking tough shit before,
but you've hardly done anything on the court.

391
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:45,040
Go for it! Kitasumi for the win!

392
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:47,540
We need to shore up our 
defense in the middle!

393
00:20:47,540 --> 00:20:49,540
Taro, don't do anything stupid this time!

394
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,540
I won't let him past me this time.

395
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,880
I didn't do all that defense 
practice for nothing!

396
00:20:56,170 --> 00:20:58,080
It doesn't matter how 
much height he has on me!

397
00:21:01,330 --> 00:21:03,790
You dumbass! She told us
to expect shots from long range!

398
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:05,750
Momoharu, get the rebound!

399
00:21:05,750 --> 00:21:07,750
Shit, you guys are running me ragged!

400
00:21:10,630 --> 00:21:12,170
He boxed him out!

401
00:21:12,420 --> 00:21:13,960
This bastard!

402
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:15,580
I can't even make him budge!

403
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:19,460
The one who taught me how to do this...
was you, Momoharu.

404
00:21:20,960 --> 00:21:21,750
Loose ball!

405
00:21:21,750 --> 00:21:22,750
What the hell?!

406
00:21:22,750 --> 00:21:24,330
You had one job, Momoharu!

407
00:21:25,830 --> 00:21:26,880
Not happening!

408
00:21:28,750 --> 00:21:30,750
Crap... he waited to shoot...!

409
00:21:36,170 --> 00:21:39,920
That little snot... he took his sweet time
to get the foul call!

410
00:21:40,380 --> 00:21:41,830
Defensive foul on #7!

411
00:21:41,830 --> 00:21:43,580
The basket counts! One free-throw!

412
00:21:44,170 --> 00:21:45,460
Holy crap...

413
00:21:45,460 --> 00:21:48,170
So, uh, that dude is starting 
to seem kind of badass.

414
00:21:56,170 --> 00:21:57,830
He's more than he seems.

415
00:21:58,290 --> 00:22:00,750
This guy is... the real deal!

416
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:35,420
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: The Best Start and the Worst Start

417
00:23:31,460 --> 00:23:35,330
Next Time: "The Best Start 
and the Worst Start."

